t]**\n\u003e \"To tackle this question, we set three detailed objectives. First, we aimed to identify the \u0027Unique Linguistic Fingerprints\u0027 of humans and four major LLMs, defining their distinct writing styles. Second, we adopted a multi-layered approach, analyzing everything from sentence structure and word choice to the deeper semantic meaning. Finally, to validate our findings, we trained a machine learning model to see if it could automatically distinguish between the authors based on these very fingerprints.\"\n\n---\n\n### **Slide 4: Data \u0026 Methodology I: A Diverse, Controlled Corpus**\n\n**[화면 구성]**\n*   **왼쪽 (1/2):** 포스터에 있는 **\"Prompt Typology\" 다이어그램**을 선명하게 배치.\n*   **오른쪽 (1/2):** 데이터 소스, 프롬프트 전략, 데이터 규모에 대한 상세한 텍스트를 배치.\n\n**[On-Screen Text]**\n\n### **Data \u0026 Methodology I: Building a Diverse and Controlled Corpus**\n\n*   **Data Sources for Comparative Analysis:**\n    *   **Human Text:** To ensure authenticity, we collected real-world, unfiltered answers from a diverse pool of human users on the Q\u0026A platform, Quora. This provides a baseline of natural human expression.\n    *   **LLM Text:** We generated responses from four leading models—Claude, DeepSeek, Gemini, and GPT—to the same set of questions posed to humans.\n\n*   **Systematic Prompting Strategy:**\n    *   To capture a wide range of response styles and avoid biases from a single prompt type, we employed five distinct prompt modes, as illustrated in the diagram.\n    *   These modes guided the AIs to produce responses that were **Minimal/Neutral, Objective/Factual, Experience-based/Subjective, and Analytical/In-depth.** This allowed us to assess not just what they write, but how their writing changes with the requested tone and purpose.\n\n*   **Dataset Scale \u0026 Composition:**\n    *   Our final dataset is built upon **100 unique questions** curated across a variety of topics to ensure generality.\n    *   We systematically sourced **30 responses per question for e